  "reviewNotes": {
    "models": "Original procedural photo-based reconstructions. Wider Wrangler bonnet and visible lettering; sampled straight G-Class door gaps, thin bonnet returns, closed front-wing webs and distinct EV/AMG front treatments. Simplified optics, interiors and front-corner transitions remain below OEM CAD/Forza fidelity.",
    "wheelMotion": "44 trials per Turning run cover nine vehicles in both directions and both full-lock directions, plus eight locked Wrangler/G63 cases. One initial rolling speed is seeded; the actual solver then coasts. Actual wheel/rim pose and loaded rolling contact are checked.",
    "brakeHolding": "Slope-gravity compensation follows the tires actually carrying load, rather than nominal four-wheel shares. Original friction and brake-torque bounds remain, with 34 additional portable incline/grip/support checks.",
    "removedDestination": "Winter Expedition travel/UI, runtime support, original authored destination maps, generated map/collision and explicit cook entries are removed. Proving-ground snow and shared acquired winter textures/meshes remain. The ordinary proving-ground out-of-world recovery boundary is retained.",
    "performance": "The previous pass15 real-time quarry diagnostic measured about 3.33 FPS with unresolved CPU physics cost. This pass did not repeat that profile or demonstrate a performance/crash fix. Fixed-clock functional runs do not establish real-time gameplay throughput.",
    "damageAndSoil": "Damage remains visual/gameplay deformation with original collision hulls; no wheel detachment or structural soft-body claim. Physical proving-ground ruts are bounded; material transitions and soil renderer configuration were not changed in this pass.",
